Spec: Change Boundary Guide

Purpose:
  Document feature-scoped Change Boundary semantics, immutable implementation authorization snapshots, lifecycle target discovery, regeneration, unresolved handling, staleness, and disposable derived-state behavior.

Owns:
  ./change-boundary.md

References:
  ../README.sdd
  ./development.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/commands/context.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/commands/validate.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/commands/authorize.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/commands/verify.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/scripts/workflow_gate.sdd

Must:
  The guide explains how target discovery becomes more precise from planning through task generation.
  The guide explains deterministic Change Boundary regeneration from canonical Spec Kit artifacts and fresh SpecDD resolver output without copying persistent SpecDD constraints.
  The guide distinguishes the refreshable feature Change Boundary from the immutable authorization snapshot recorded after successful authorization.
  The guide distinguishes advisory unresolved planning context from unresolved implementation authority that cannot grant permission.
  The guide explains when a Change Boundary is refreshed, when authorization records its exact validated state, and why later refreshes do not alter current-operation authority.
  The guide explains stale-boundary conditions and the required refresh plus reauthorization points after deliberate evolution.
  The guide presents `boundary.json` as disposable derived state and the authorization snapshot as generated historical operation evidence.
  Installation and development-host maintenance remain delegated to the README and development guide rather than duplicated here.

Done when:
  A maintainer can determine when a Change Boundary is created or refreshed, when authorization snapshots it, which state verification uses, and how a new authority context begins after evolution.
